SC2SLR: supply the missing AlphaPose keypoint glue

Why: main.py imports AlphaPose.get_image_keypoint and dataset/dataloader_video.py
imports AlphaPose.keypoint_to_heatmap.get_heatmap, but AlphaPose/ is in the
released .gitignore and neither module exists in the commit, in upstream
AlphaPose, or anywhere GitHub code search reaches. Without them the code fails
at import (preference level 1 is impossible).

What the reconstruction does (each item is a documented guess, recorded in
reproduction.json.guesses_and_deviations):
- Keypoint_getter serves Halpe-136 keypoints that AlphaPose computed once per
  frame (modal_app.py extract_keypoints) instead of running AlphaPose inside
  the data loader on every augmented frame of every epoch, which would mean
  ~10^8 detector+pose passes. It keeps the paper's 90 keypoints (Sec. 3.2:
  7 upper body, 9 nose, 12 eye, 20 mouth, 42 hand).
- render_heatmap draws confidence-weighted Gaussians (sigma 4 px at 256x256,
  max over keypoints) - the (T,224,224) heatmap the released normalize() adds
  to the video. The heatmap is rendered before augmentation as a 4th channel,
  so the released crop and temporal-rescale transforms move it with the frames;
  normalize() splits it off again exactly where the released code calls
  get_heatmap. Nothing else in the released fusion changes.
Applies to: https://github.com/christianlsl/Skeleton-based-Contrast-for-Sign-Language-Recognition @ 65c95fb03fa0c170dc3f1136265f4b97ec26d7fa (git apply from the repo root)
